  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Tuppenny Ha'penny Loo. Players hold 5 cards and 5 buttons. In turn each plays one card face down; matching the previous rank costs the previous player 1 to 3 buttons (escalating). Last player with buttons wins.",
    Player: "Tuppenny Ha'penny Loo is a simple matching/penalty card game. Players hold 5 cards and 5 buttons. Cards are played face down in turn; if the next player matches the rank, the previous player pays buttons to the pot. Consecutive matches escalate the penalty (1, 2, 3 buttons). Player who runs out of buttons loses.",
    objective: "Be the last player with buttons. Avoid matching the previous card's rank when playing, since matching forces the previous player to pay buttons into the pot; consecutive matches escalate (1, then 2, then 3 buttons).",
    gameplay: 'Play cards face down in sequence. If next player matches rank of previous card: previous player pays 1 button. Second consecutive match: 2 buttons. Third: 3 buttons. Play all 5 cards per round. Player out of buttons loses.',
    keyRules: [
      'Match rank = penalty',
      'Escalating penalties for consecutive matches',
      '5 buttons starting stake',
    ],
